  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State Of Mah. Thr.F.I. Chandrpur vs Kisan Guddiji Kunkulwar on 3 April, 2018 Author: Rohit B. Deo Bench: Rohit B. Deo 1 apeal715.0 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay, Nagpur Bench, Nagpur. Criminal Appeal No.715 Of 2003 State of Maharashtra, through Food Inspector, Food & Drugs Administration Department, M.S. Chandrapur.",
    "facts": "Food Inspector, Chandrapur Shri A.S. Dhule accompanied by panch Kisan Shende visited the grocery shop of the accused at village Rajoli, Tahsil - Mul at 12-15 p.m. on 19-1-1994. Shri A.S. Dhule disclosed his identity and conveyed that he wished to take sample of groundnut oil and gram dal for the purpose of analysis. Shri A.S. Dhule purchased 450 gram groundnut oil from a packed tin of 15 kg. in the presence of the panch. He also purchased 750 gram dal. Notice in form 14-A was given to the accused and an acknowledgment obtained. The groundnut oil was divided in three equal parts and each part was poured in separate clean glass bottles. Each bottle was sealed with cork and wrapped in thick paper. One part of the sample was sent 3 apeal715.03 to the Public Analysis, Pune who submitted report dated 22-2-1994 to the effect that the sample did not confer to the standards prescribed in the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. The chana dal which was purchased from the shop was also divided in three equal parts and poured in three clean dry empty plastic containers which were sealed by lead. The sample label was signed by the Food Inspector, the panch witness Kisan Shende and the accused. One part of the sample was analyzed and the report dated 22-2-194 opines that the sample did not confirm to the standard of chana dal as per the Rules. The case of the prosecution is that vide letter dated 04-4-1994 submitted to the Food Inspector Shri Ghule, the accused disclosed that he did not purchase Deepak Brand Groundnut Oil. The Food Inspector obtained the statutory sanction of the Act and filed a complaint on 29-6-1995. 4 apeal715.03 5.",
    "arguments": "8. Shri M.P. Khajanchi would submit, that there is no evidence on record to suggest that the sample collected was of representative character in the absence of evidence that the oil was stirred.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "8. Shri M.P. Khajanchi would submit, that there is no evidence on record to suggest that the sample collected was of representative character in the absence of evidence that the oil was stirred.",
